@@ -240,6 +240,28 @@ Variable parts are of course also possible in the host section::
     ], host_matching=True)
 
 
+Subdomain Matching
+==================
+
+.. versionchanged:: 3.2
+    Subdomain matching must be enabled with ``subdomain_matching=True``.
+
+To match on the subdomain part of the host instead, pass
+``subdomain_matching=True`` to the :class:`Map` constructor, give rules a
+``subdomain`` argument, and pass the ``server_name`` the subdomain is relative
+to when binding::
+
+    url_map = Map([
+        Rule('/', endpoint='www_index', subdomain='www'),
+        Rule('/', endpoint='help_index', subdomain='help')
+    ], subdomain_matching=True)
+    urls = url_map.bind_to_environ(environ, server_name='example.com')
+
+If it is not enabled, :meth:`Map.bind_to_environ` will not extract the
+subdomain from the host, and the ``server_name`` will only be used when
+building external URLs.
+
+
 WebSockets
